{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/3D Manipulation.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/3D Manipulation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"3 d manipulation 3 d manipulation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/3D Manipulation.md","fileName":"3D Manipulation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"3D Manipulation","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Spatial Interaction]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Interaction","Interaction Technique","Object Selection","Object Positioning","Object Rotation","Object Scaling","Input Device","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/3D Manipulation.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/3D Manipulation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"3 d manipulation 3 d manipulation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/3D Manipulation.md","fileName":"3D Manipulation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"3D Manipulation","heading":"3D Manipulation","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"3D manipulation uses an [[Interaction Technique]] to map user input into changes to objects in a three-dimensional environment. For design and evaluation, it is commonly narrowed to manipulation of spatial rigid objects whose shape is preserved.\n\nCanonical tasks include [[Object Selection]], [[Object Positioning]], [[Object Rotation]], and [[Object Scaling]]. Each task has parameters such as target distance, size, surrounding density, required precision, and amount of movement. Application-specific tasks may add constraints that these canonical tasks do not capture.\n\nTechnique quality depends on the task, [[Input Device]], display, user, and environment. There is no single best manipulation technique for every application.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Interaction","Interaction Technique","Obje